# Lychee ignore list — known false-positives or transient issues.
#
# Format: one URL pattern (regex) per line. See https://lychee.cli.rs/usage/config/
#
# Process for adding entries:
# 1. Run the weekly link-audit workflow (or lychee locally) and inspect failures.
# 2. For genuine false-positives (sites that block the checker, paywalls,
#    rate-limited-but-live, malformed-but-reachable), add a comment-justified entry.
# 3. For genuine dead links, prefer fixing the source over suppressing here.

# --- Valid links the checker can't fetch (sites up, but block bots / send
#     malformed responses / TLS quirks). Reviewed manually — keep the links. ---
eci\.gov\.in
ev\.delhi\.gov\.in
ocmms\.nic\.in
safar\.tropmet\.res\.in
main\.sci\.gov\.in
cpcb\.nic\.in


# --- Publisher / news / data portals that load fine in a browser but return
#     400 / 415 (Accept-header negotiation) or bot-block automated checkers even
#     with a browser User-Agent + Accept header. Surfaced by the July 2026 audit
#     (issue #176); each verified reachable manually. Prefer keeping the citation. ---
sciencedirect\.com
science\.org
link\.springer\.com
iqair\.com
business-standard\.com
downtoearth\.org\.in
teriin\.org
ilo\.org
mospi\.gov\.in
news\.webindia123\.com

# --- CHANGELOG compare/release links for early versions never tagged on GitHub (v24/v25). ---
github\.com/JanVayu/JanVayu/(compare|releases/tag)/v2[45]\.
